## Context
Child of tracker 1317 (forge leaks). The landing path is the highest-stakes surface: a raw
`gh` call here makes a no-forge or other-forge repository fail, or read "nothing found" as a
clear. Model: `scripts/forge.py` (gh and none backends, typed NOOP and refusal, offline cache),
`tests/test_forge.py`; the none backend's state is `review_notes.py` (refs/notes/review) and
`merge-gate.py` (refs/notes/gate).

Sites on main 2026-10-28:
- `skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh` (~342 `gh pr view --json state`, ~360 auto-merge armed read)
- `skills/roar/check-close-claims.sh` (~56 `gh pr list --state merged`)
- `scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh` (~100-133: open PR list, repo view, PR files)
- `scripts/review-anchor.py` (~31, error text naming `gh pr view`; check whether any raw call remains)

Shell callers need a CLI: today `forge.py` exposes only `resolve`. This child sets the CLI
shape (subcommands over the existing backend methods) that 1319 and 1320 build on.

Parent: tracker 1317.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The four sites above call `forge.py` (Python API or CLI) instead of `gh`, or are listed
      in this ticket's log as residue with a reason
- [ ] Each ported site has a `none`-backend test (no `gh` on PATH) showing the step still
      works or answers a typed NOOP/refusal, never an empty all-clear
- [ ] A verb or CLI subcommand is added to `scripts/forge.py` only where a caller here needs it,
      with its gh and none behaviour tested in `tests/test_forge.py`
- [ ] `make check` passes
